<%- cpus = user_context["cpu"].to_s.strip -%>
<%- mem  = user_context["memory"].to_s.strip -%>
<%- unless cpus.empty? || mem.empty? -%>
**Resources:** <%= cpus %> CPU<%= "s" unless cpus == "1" %>, <%= mem %> GB
<%- end -%>

Each browser tab is its own login shell, and closing the tab ends it — the same
as closing an ssh connection. Use `tmux` or `screen` for anything that has to
outlive the tab.

Run `bao-getkey` once per session, then `ssh derecho` or `ssh casper` (and
`qsub` there) without the two-factor prompt.

The session ends itself an hour after the last tab is closed, so closing your
tabs releases the CPU and memory rather than holding them.
